commit 3b23578f38d20ccee2fff6cd5778448daab05a58
Author: Beacon <info@lucernaread.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 22:33:45 2026 +0000

    tools: occlusion_audit Cyrillic font mapping + ink_box whitespace-edge fix (pre-insert W47)
    
    resolve_font mapped every 'Noto Serif'/'Noto Sans' run to the CJK SC
    face, but the build (core-ru svglib._char_font) renders Cyrillic runs
    with the non-CJK Noto Serif/Sans: the CJK face overstates Cyrillic ink
    ~2-6% (+3.0-8.0px per word; Bold 53 'Zenit' 171.8 vs build 166.3) and
    raised 42 false TEXTX flags on W47 ru-nl. resolve_font now takes the
    run's text and diverts Cyrillic runs in the bare families to the
    non-CJK Noto faces; 'Noto Serif/Sans CJK SC' and Latin/CJK mappings
    are unchanged (control group byte-identical).
    
    ink_box measured getbbox() on the raw string, but PIL counts a
    whitespace glyph's degenerate (zero-height, full-advance-wide) box as
    ink at the edges: '» ' reports 12.5px wider than '»' at 53pt, a
    leading U+3000 adds a full em (46px at 46pt) to '\u3000TAAL'. ink_box
    now measures the stripped core and shifts it by the stripped leading
    prefix's advance. Seam gaps on the 42-flag sample go from
    -5.25..-3.00px to -0.25..+0.15px, matching the per-glyph serial
    ground truth (-0.08..+0.16px); audit on ru-nl and core-ru: 42 -> 0
    flags; ru-en: 42 -> 0; en-fr/en-ja/zh-tw-ru unchanged (0); selftest
    still green.

